# Do not manage the dev server

The user **always** runs `quasar dev` outside Cursor. It hot-restarts on file changes.

## Never do this

- `quasar dev`, `npm run dev`, `npx quasar dev`
- `kill` / `pkill` on dev-server PIDs
- Background dev-server launches from the agent
- `curl localhost:…` to “verify” the running server (assumes agent control)
- “Restart the dev server” or “hard refresh” as a troubleshooting step

## Instead

- Make code/config fixes and **stop** — the external dev server picks them up
- If a change needs a restart the agent cannot trigger, **tell the user** in one line; do not run server commands
- Use file reads, builds (`npm run build`), or tests — not live-server probes
